add(36,"The Empire of Zul'Drak",{
    "Start at Light's Breach and complete its rescue/fire/troll quests for Finding Allies. Follow Crusader Forward Camp to Gymer's rescue and The Storm King's Vengeance. Use Gymer's vehicle actions and healing pickups; finish the full Storm King's Crusade turn-in.",
    "At Ebon Watch, start Stefan Vadu's Kickin' Nass and Takin' Manes. Loot the Unliving Choker to start An Invitation of Sorts, then follow the disguise chain into Voltarus. Alternate Drakuru's tasks with Stefan's sabotage work, using Stefan's horn to summon him when required. Finish Betrayal and loot Drakuru's skull.",
    "At the Argent Stand, complete Pa'Troll and each captain's assignment, including Lab Work. Continue the Captain Rupert/Dr. Rogers rescue and spider chains through Malas the Corrupter for The Argent Patrol. Check the camp east of the stand if its chapter remains missing.",
    "For Sseratus, loot Strange Mojo from the altar trolls and follow Hexxer Ubungo's Precious Elemental Fluids, Mushroom Mixer and Too Much of a Good Thing. Combine the elemental links and use the resulting item as the quest instructs.",
    "Continue through Zim'Torga to Har'koa, Rhunok and Quetz'lun. Finish the linked gods' chains, including the underworld spirit interactions, through You Reap What You Sow. Then complete the Key of Warlord Zol'Maz, Rampage, The Gods Have Spoken and Convocation at Zol'Heb for Akali.",
    "At the Amphitheater of Anguish, take and turn in EACH arena challenge in order: Yggdras, Magnataur, From Beyond, Tuskarrmageddon, Korrak and the Champion of Anguish. Check all eight chapters. The current achievement uses these endings, not the old 100-quest total.",
},{pin(121,32,75,1,"Light's Breach - Finding Allies"),pin(121,19.7,56.3,1,"Gymer - Storm King's Crusade"),pin(121,14,73,2,"Ebon Watch - Stefan and the Unliving Choker"),pin(121,28,45,2,"Voltarus - disguise and Drakuru tasks"),pin(121,39.4,67,3,"Argent Stand - Pa'Troll"),pin(121,58,72.6,3,"Captain Rupert - rescue/spider chain"),pin(121,59,57,5,"Zim'Torga - gods' storylines"),pin(121,48.5,56.4,6,"Amphitheater of Anguish - complete all rounds")},storyTip,{2557578,6239393})
add(38,"The Summit of Storm Peaks",{
    "Start at K3 and finish Defending K3. Follow Gretchen Fizzlespark's They Took Our Men! chain into the disguised Brunnhildar village. Complete its bear, prisoner and drake-competition sequence through the Thorim introduction and Mending Fences.",
    "Continue Thorim's story and repair your standing with the Sons of Hodir. Finish the yellow quest chain through The Reckoning for Heartbreak/Loken and the Sons of Hodir chapter; repeatable reputation turn-ins alone do not replace the storyline.",
    "Complete the faction branch from Frosthold (Alliance) or Grom'arsh Crash-Site/Camp Tunka'lo (Horde). Follow the Frostborn king or Stormhoof story, and the Iron Colossus/Norgannon quests, checking which faction-specific criteria your character sees.",
    "Follow the Brann/Creteus investigation and Pursuing a Legend branches to their final hand-ins. On Horde, follow Xarantaur, the Witness to Camp Tunka'lo and complete The Witness and the Hero and its scroll investigation. Check Brann's Communicator in your bags if no NPC marker appears.",
    "Finish Bearly Ready and The Harpy Problem through the remaining Brunnhildar/Frosthold side chains, then review every current chapter tick. Flying access is useful for this mountainous route. The old Engineering-only SCRAP-E quest and an exact 100-quest count are not required by the chapter system.",
},{pin(120,41.1,86.1,1,"K3 - Gretchen and Defending K3"),pin(120,50.9,65.6,1,"Brunnhildar - disguised village chain"),pin(120,33.4,58,2,"Temple of Storms - Thorim's story"),pin(120,65,60,2,"Dun Niffelem - Sons of Hodir"),pin(120,29.5,74,3,"Frosthold - Alliance story branch"),pin(120,36.5,49,3,"Grom'arsh Crash-Site - Horde story branch"),pin(120,65.4,50.8,3,"Camp Tunka'lo - Stormhoof / investigation")},storyTip,{2548217,2558231,3226854,5600357})
add(39,"Into the Basin",{
    "At Nesingwary Base Camp in Sholazar Basin, complete the engine/repair introduction, then the rhino, dreadsaber and crocolisk mastery chains. Follow Hemet's In Search of Bigger Game to Dorian Drakestalker's camp and finish the mammoth/dragon conclusion for Hunting Bigger Game and Teeth, Spikes, and Talons.",
    "At the Avatar of Freya in the northeast, follow her Scourge, pillar and Lifewarden work. Finish the late Lifewarden/Waygate turn-ins rather than stopping at Trust of a Lifewarden. These complete The Lifewarden and Watching Over the Basin.",
    "For The Wolvar, kill Pitch at 50.6, 76.8 and immediately accept Playing Along from Tracker Gekgek. Work through the Frenzyheart chain. If progression disappears, use Goregek's Shackles from your bags, or ask Elder Harkek at Frenzyheart Hill for a replacement.",
    "Continue the injured Oracle rescue and the Rainspeaker Canopy storyline. Use Lafoo's Bug Bag or the other supplied Oracle summon item for quests that do not appear over a fixed NPC. Ask High-Oracle Soo-say for a replacement if needed.",
    "Continue the Oracle investigation through the cave confrontation with Artruis and A Hero's Burden where offered. Check all six story chapters. You do not need both factions Exalted for Into the Basin; that is the separate Mercenary of Sholazar achievement.",
},{pin(119,27,58.5,1,"Nesingwary Base Camp - hunting chains"),pin(119,42.3,28.7,1,"Dorian's camp - bigger game and mammoth"),pin(119,64.5,48.6,2,"Avatar of Freya - pillar/Lifewarden chain"),pin(119,50.6,76.8,3,"Pitch - kill and accept Playing Along"),pin(119,55,69,3,"Frenzyheart Hill - Elder Harkek / summon item"),pin(119,54.6,56.3,4,"Rainspeaker Canopy - Oracle summon items"),pin(119,70.8,58.7,5,"Artruis's cave - faction-choice conclusion")},storyTip,{550180,566964,833336,2562775})
add(40,"Icecrown: The Final Goal",{
    "Begin at Argent Vanguard, not the raid entrance. Complete Tirion's defense chain: Honor Above All Else, the rescue/Skytalon work, A Cold Front Approaches, The Last Line of Defense, then the Scourgeholme campaign and The Battle for Crusaders' Pinnacle. Finish In Defiance of the Scourge.",
    "Take the introduction to your faction's moving airship, Skybreaker or Orgrim's Hammer. Talk to ALL its quest givers even when they show blue daily markers: they can also offer necessary yellow quests. Follow Broken Front/Mord'rethar and the Retest Now/It's All Fun and Games branch to Baron Sliver. Finish I Have an Idea, But First..., Free Your Mind and If He Cannot Be Turned to capture The Shadow Vault.",
    "At the captured Shadow Vault, finish the Death's Rise/Grand Admiral work for What's Yours Is Mine. Follow Keritose Bloodblade's Parting Gifts, vehicle and saronite chains through Amidst the Confusion for Seizing Saronite. Continue to Vereth the Cunning, New Recruit, the Lithe Seeker missions and the three Riders through The Fate of Bloodbane for Malykriss.",
    "For The Unthinkable, follow The Leaper to the Bone Witch. In the Underhalls (entrance 32.45, 31.89), loot Apprentice Osterkilgr's key quest and finish The Sum Is Greater than the Parts. Complete the Bone Witch's Water Terror, ancient hero and Banshee's Revenge chain, then each Battle at Valhalas challenge in order.",
    "At Blackwatch (35.4, 66.3), follow Darkrider Arly and Crusader Olakin: Where Are They Coming From?, Destroying the Altars, Jagged Shards, the doctor/reassembly sequence, and The Flesh Giant Champion. Use the quest's vehicle and body-part interactions, and wait for the reassembly dialogue. This finishes Teaching the Meaning of Fear.",
    "Return to the airship for the Matthias Lehner investigation. Follow the Ymirheim mine and later Lehner appearances through Army of the Damned, Futility, Where Dragons Fell, The Hunter and the Prince, Knowledge Is a Terrible Burden and Argent Aid. Finish Tirion's Gambit under the cultist disguise, following Tirion through the whole scene for The Heart of the Lich King.",
    "At Tirion, start A Tale of Valor and visit Crusader Bridenbrad. Complete all three attempts to save him: Keeper Remulos in Moonglade, Alexstrasza in Dragonblight, and A'dal in Shattrath. Use the offered quest portals when available. Return each boon to Bridenbrad and finish the chest's Light Within the Darkness.",
    "Back on the faction airship, check Thassarian (Alliance) or Koltira (Horde) for the later Aldur'thar and Corp'rethar orders. Finish Drag and Drop, Not a Bug, Need More Info and No Rest for the Wicked; then Raise the Barricades, the Ironwall/sky campaign and The Guardians of Corp'rethar/Shatter the Shards. Keep checking the CURRENT chapter list and final hand-ins.",
},{pin(118,87,76.9,1,"Argent Vanguard - Tirion's original campaign"),pin(118,80,72,1,"Crusaders' Pinnacle - finish the defense chain"),pin(125,69.7,45.4,2,"Krasus' Landing - faction-airship introduction"),pin(118,43.5,25.2,2,"Shadow Vault - capture before later chains"),pin(118,20.3,47.8,3,"Death's Rise - Grand Admiral branch"),pin(118,32.45,31.89,4,"Underhalls entrance - Osterkilgr / Nergeld"),pin(118,35.4,66.3,5,"Blackwatch - Arly and Olakin"),pin(118,71.54,37.5,6,"Matthias Lehner - Where Dragons Fell"),pin(118,44.45,76.17,6,"Tirion's Gambit - disguised meeting"),pin(118,79.8,30.8,7,"Crusader Bridenbrad - three boons"),pin(80,36.2,41.8,7,"Keeper Remulos - Moonglade boon"),pin(115,59.8,54.6,7,"Alexstrasza - Wyrmrest Temple boon"),pin(111,54,44.5,7,"A'dal - Shattrath boon"),pin(118,51.93,33.29,8,"Aldur'thar interior - No Rest for the Wicked")},
    storyTip.." Stay on one character for the interconnected campaign when possible. Its phase and hub unlocks are character-specific even when Warband chapter credit is shared. Airships move: use their world-map icons rather than a fixed ground pin. Argent Tournament dailies do not finish these chapters.",
    {2558388,2558389,2567129,5982305,6241328})

add(41,"Loremaster of Northrend",{
    "Track the eight zone-story achievements: Borean Tundra, Howling Fjord, Dragonblight, Grizzly Hills, Zul'Drak, Sholazar Basin, Storm Peaks and Icecrown. The Retail criteria are completed STORY CHAPTERS, not a fixed total of random quests.",
    "Work through one zone's complete guide before starting another. Follow the appropriate faction variant in the four split-faction zones. Enable Trivial Quests and keep quest-starting/summoning items until their story branches are finished.",
    "Plan flying access for Storm Peaks and complete Icecrown's hub-unlock campaign on one character where practical. Warband credit can combine zone achievements, but it does not unlock another character's phased quest givers.",
    "Check the meta after all eight zones credit. Crystalsong Forest and Wintergrasp exploration are not additional quest-story requirements. If a chapter is missing, use that zone guide's specific late-chain and bag-item corrections.",
},{pin(114,58.5,68.2,2,"Borean Tundra"),pin(117,59.9,64.5,2,"Howling Fjord"),pin(115,59.8,54.6,2,"Dragonblight"),pin(116,31.8,60,2,"Grizzly Hills"),pin(121,32,75,2,"Zul'Drak"),pin(119,27,58.5,2,"Sholazar Basin"),pin(120,41.1,86.1,3,"Storm Peaks"),pin(118,87,76.9,3,"Icecrown - Argent Vanguard")},nil,{1957237,2567334,6085224})

add(547,"Veteran of the Wrathgate",{
    "Enable Trivial Quests and follow your faction's Dragonblight campaign. ALLIANCE: begin The Lost Courier at Stars' Rest and continue Of Traitors and Treason to High Commander Halford Wyrmbane at Wintergarde. Finish Naxxramas and the Fall of Wintergarde, Flight of the Wintergarde Defender and Return to the High Commander.",
    "ALLIANCE: finish BOTH Wintergarde branches. Rescue from Town Square leads through Find Durkon!, The Noble's Crypt, the clickable Secrets of the Scourge tome, Mystery of the Tome and A Righteous Sermon. The Demo-gnome leads through The Search for Slinkin, Leave Nothing to Chance and Understanding the Scourge War Machine. Replies correct The Bleeding Ore: complete it too if the next quest is locked.",
    "ALLIANCE: follow Into Hostile Territory, Steamtank Surprise, Scattered to the Wind, The Chain Gun And You, Plunderbeard's journal and both Chasing Icestorm quests through Finality. Continue An End And A Beginning and To Fordragon Hold! to Audience With The Dragon Queen.",
    "HORDE: start Into the Fold/Blood Oath of the Horde, then report to Agmar's Hammer. Finish Victory Nears through Blightbeasts be Damned, and the Strength of Icemist/Chains of the Anub'ar/Return of the High Chief branch through All Hail Roanauk!.",
    "HORDE: complete the Venomspite plague branch: Imbeciles Abound!, The Forsaken Blight and You, Emerald Dragon Tears, Spread the Good Word and The Forsaken Blight. Continue The Kor'kron Vanguard! and Audience With The Dragon Queen.",
    "BOTH FACTIONS: at Wyrmrest Temple finish Galakrond and the Scourge, then use the Ruby Beacon's dragon for On Ruby Wings. Continue Return to Angrathar to the Wrathgate and finish the cinematic/turn-in for achievement credit.",
},{pin(115,29,55,1,"Stars' Rest - Alliance Lost Courier"),pin(115,78,48,2,"Wintergarde - BOTH military branches"),pin(115,37.8,23.4,3,"Fordragon Hold - Alliance final introduction"),pin(115,38,46,4,"Agmar's Hammer - Horde military/Taunka"),pin(115,76.5,62.5,5,"Venomspite - Horde plague branch"),pin(115,59.8,54.6,6,"Wyrmrest Temple - Dragon Queen"),pin(115,38.5,19.5,6,"Angrathar - Wrathgate conclusion")},"Use only your faction's branches. The old Battle for Undercity follow-up was removed; it is not needed for this still-obtainable achievement.",{387111,447601,1182131,1191185})
add(561,"D.E.H.T.A's Little P.I.T.A.",{
    "Visit the D.E.H.T.A. camp in Borean Tundra (57.1, 44.3), enable Trivial Quests and accept its parallel tasks. Avoid killing protected wildlife while working for the camp; if Animal Blood makes the druids hostile, wait for it to clear before approaching.",
    "Complete Ears of Our Enemies by collecting 15 Nesingwary Lackey Ears from the poachers. Also finish Ned, Lord of Rhinos... by killing Nedar and Lunchbox. Further repeatable ear turn-ins do not replace the one-time chains.",
    "Finish the mammoth branch: Help Those That Cannot Help Themselves (free eight calves), Khu'nok Will Know (escort the calf), then Kaw the Mammoth Destroyer. Use the supplied quest interactions/vehicle and take Kaw's War Halberd.",
    "Finish the caribou branch: Unfit for Death (trap eight Nesingwary Trappers), then The Culler Cometh. Use the traps as instructed rather than killing the rescued animals.",
    "Finish the clam branch: Happy as a Clam, The Abandoned Reach, Not On Our Watch (12 animal-part shipments), and The Nefarious Clam Master.... Follow Hierophant Liandra's coastal follow-ups as well as the original camp tasks.",
    "Return to Arch Druid Lathorius and TALK to him even if his marker is blue for repeatable ears. Accept The Assassination of Harold Lane, kill Lane at the far side of Lake Kum'uya and turn it in. If the final quest is missing, check all branches and the initial ear turn-in before grinding unrelated reputation.",
},{pin(114,57.1,44.3,1,"D.E.H.T.A. - all parallel rescue chains"),pin(114,57.1,44.3,2,"Lathorius - initial ear turn-in"),pin(114,59.5,30.6,3,"Khu'nok - mammoth chain"),pin(114,57.8,55.1,5,"Abandoned Reach - Liandra's coastal chain"),pin(114,49.4,40.4,6,"Lake Kum'uya - Harold Lane")},nil,{334612,1383285})
add(938,"The Snows of Northrend",{
    "At Nesingwary Base Camp in Sholazar Basin (27, 58), finish Weslex Quickwrench's Need an Engine, Take an Engine and Have a Part, Give a Part. Complete Debaar's Venture Co. Misadventure and Wipe That Grin Off His Face to unlock the hunting branches.",
    "Finish ALL three mastery chains: Hemet's Rhino Mastery: The Test / The Chase, An Offering for Soo-rahm, The Bones of Nozronn and Rhino Mastery: The Kill; Buck Cantwell's Dreadsaber Mastery through Ready to Pounce; and Debaar's Crocolisk Mastery through The Ambush. Soo-rahm is near 25, 66 if that follow-up is missing.",
    "Take Hemet's In Search of Bigger Game and report to Dorian Drakestalker near the Savage Thicket (42.3, 28.7). Complete Securing the Bait and Sharpening Your Talons.",
    "At Dorian's camp complete Zootfizzle's A Mammoth Undertaking. Use its quest interaction to bring back a mammoth. Replies establish that My Pet Roc and Reagent Agent are optional for the achievement's final hunt.",
    "Accept Dorian's Post-partum Aggression, carry out the quest's mammoth/dragon attack and return for the final turn-in. Killing random basin wildlife or only finishing the three early mastery chains is insufficient.",
},{pin(119,27,58.5,1,"Nesingwary Base Camp - engine and Venture Co. prerequisites"),pin(119,25,66,2,"Soo-rahm - rhino mastery follow-up"),pin(119,42.3,28.7,3,"Dorian's camp - bigger game"),pin(119,42.3,28.7,4,"Zootfizzle - A Mammoth Undertaking"),pin(119,42.3,28.7,5,"Dorian - Post-partum Aggression")},nil,{548389})
add(1596,"Guru of Drakuru",{
    "In Grizzly Hills visit Drakuru in the cage at Granite Springs (16.2, 47.5) and start Truce?. Continue Vial of Visions, Subject to Interpretation, Sacrifices Must Be Made, Heart of the Ancients, My Old Enemy and Voices From the Dust. Keep the vial/summoning items and use them at the quest's named braziers.",
    "Accept Cleansing Drak'Tharon, enter Drak'Tharon Keep and clear to the last boss, The Prophet Tharon'ja. Use the Elixir of Visions at Drakuru's brazier in the final area, finish his scene and turn in the quest. Merely killing Tharon'ja does not finish this half.",
    "For the Zul'Drak half, visit Ebon Watch (14, 73). Complete Stefan Vadu's introduction, obtain the Unliving Choker quest-starting drop and follow An Invitation of Sorts into the Scourge disguise/Voltarus chain.",
    "Alternate Drakuru's orders in Voltarus with Stefan's sabotage quests. Use Stefan's horn where required and keep the quest disguise/item. Continue through the scouting, Blight and Servant of Drakuru tasks until Betrayal is offered.",
    "Complete Betrayal's encounter and turn-in, including its quest interactions and Drakuru's skull. Check BOTH Cleansing Drak'Tharon and Betrayal criteria. If the former completed without credit, leave the dungeon and log out/back in; recent Retail comments still report delayed credit after relogging.",
},{pin(116,16.2,47.5,1,"Granite Springs - Truce? and Drakuru's vial"),pin(121,28.6,86.9,2,"Drak'Tharon Keep - Cleansing Drak'Tharon"),pin(121,14,73,3,"Ebon Watch - Stefan / Unliving Choker"),pin(121,28,45,4,"Voltarus - Drakuru and sabotage chain"),pin(121,28,45,5,"Voltarus - Betrayal conclusion")},"The two halves can be completed in either order. Do not discard a summons item just because there is no visible fixed-NPC quest marker.",{450885,1407617,1753093,5786605,6182017})
add(1254,"Friend or Fowl?",{
    "Travel to the turkey field west of Explorers' League Outpost in Howling Fjord, around 69.2, 64.6. Find a fresh group of Fjord Turkeys and put a fast, appropriate damage ability on an easy key.",
    "Kill one turkey to start the three-minute window, then move immediately between the nearby packs. Kill FIFTEEN Fjord Turkeys before time expires; do not spend the window travelling between distant areas.",
    "Use a targeting button such as /targetexact Fjord Turkey to find nearby survivors, then attack them yourself. In Chromie Time their scaled health may require a real attack rather than a tiny low-level hit.",
    "Check the kill count and achievement. If another player recently cleared the field, wait for enough respawns before restarting. Do Critter Gitter first if you also want to feed the living turkeys.",
},{pin(117,69.2,64.6,1,"Fjord Turkey field - west of Explorers' League Outpost"),pin(117,69.2,64.6,2,"Kill 15 Fjord Turkeys within three minutes")},nil,{462280,6018883})
add(1277,"Rapid Defense",{
    "Unlock Defending Wyrmrest Temple through the Dragonblight dragonshrine chain. If the Shimmering Shard does not drop, first finish Rifle the Bodies (Horde, 11999; Alliance, 12000), then follow its shard investigation and Wyrmrest introductions.",
    "Find the daily on Wyrmrest Temple's MIDDLE/SECOND floor, accessible from the west around 58, 54. This is above the ground transport NPCs and below the Dragon Queen, not the basement raid entrance. Track Rapid Defense before accepting the daily: its THREE-minute timer starts at acceptance.",
    "Immediately board a nearby Wyrmrest Defender. Fly toward the Azure Dragonshrine southwest of the temple and use Destabilize the Azure Dragonshrine (vehicle action 5) over the quest target. Wait for objective credit rather than assuming the button cooldown means success.",
    "While moving, kill three Azure Dragons and five Azure Drakes. Use Immolate (2) followed by Fireball (1), prioritizing wounded enemies fighting friendly NPCs; current high-level vehicle damage can make this much quicker than the old comments describe. Renew (3) heals your vehicle and the speed action (4) helps with travel.",
    "Once all objectives credit, speed back to the SAME middle-floor quest giver. EXIT the vehicle and finish the turn-in before three minutes. Completing the kills within the timer but handing in late is not enough; abandon/reaccept before completion if an attempt clearly fails.",
},{pin(115,38,46,1,"Agmar's Hammer - Horde dragonshrine introduction"),pin(115,29,55,1,"Stars' Rest - Alliance dragonshrine introduction"),pin(115,58,54,2,"Wyrmrest Temple MIDDLE floor - accept timed daily"),pin(115,55.5,66.2,3,"Azure Dragonshrine - vehicle destabilization target"),pin(115,58,54,5,"Return, exit drake and turn in before three minutes")},"Do the timed daily outside a raid group. Old two-minute instructions, old camera commands and obsolete quest-completion macros are omitted.",{446096,1385789,1810446,6285532})
add(1428,"Mine Sweeper",{
    "Go to the Sparksocket Minefield just west of K3 in Storm Peaks (about 36, 86). Track Mine Sweeper and use the safe path toward the center, the same approach used for Just Around the Corner.",
    "Pick two nearby clusters on opposite sides of the center and step/jump onto a mine to begin. As you rise, identify the next mine and turn your camera/character so you can move straight toward it when control returns.",
    "On descent, aim to land near another mine. If you touch the ground, immediately run into the next one: there is a short grace period, so brief contact need not ruin the chain. Avoid running out of the minefield or waiting between explosions.",
    "Keep criss-crossing between clusters, approaching mines from an angle that tends to send you back into the field. Your facing alone does not guarantee the blast direction; adjust to the actual launch and choose your next mine while airborne.",
    "Chain TEN detonations before the counter resets. If a gap resets progress, return to a dense cluster and restart. Between launches, touch the ground briefly near the next mine and adjust your approach angle to keep the chain going.",
},{pin(120,36,86,1,"Sparksocket Minefield - center approach"),pin(120,36,86,2,"Begin a mine chain in the dense central field"),pin(120,36,86,5,"Chain ten detonations with minimal gaps")},"Recent mount/flight-method reports conflict between patches. The route uses the ground/air control method; no Engineering item, specific mount or flight exploit is required.",{532255,6058426,6314030,6440358})

add(1956,"Higher Learning",{
    "In ORIGINAL Northrend Dalaran, track Higher Learning and visit all eight book spawns below. Read the full title: an unrelated book in the same spot is a placeholder. Read placeholders too to clear them, then repeat the circuit after respawns.",
    "Introduction: enter the Violet Gate portal room (56.7, 46.1) and inspect the floor beside its northern/right bookcase.",
    "Conjuration: inside the Violet Citadel (30.9, 46.3), inspect the bottom of the bookcase on your right on the entrance floor.",
    "Divination: go UPSTAIRS in the Violet Citadel (26.5, 51.7), near the Caverns of Time portal area, and check the floor by the shelves.",
    "Enchantment: enter Threads of Fate (43.6, 47.1), climb upstairs and go onto its balcony. Check the crate outside.",
    "Transmutation: inspect the ground-floor western bookcase near the entrance/stove in the Legerdemain Lounge (46.9, 39.8).",
    "Necromancy: go UPSTAIRS in the same lounge (46.9, 39.1), into the western bedroom, and inspect the empty bookcase. This is a separate spawn from Transmutation.",
    "Abjuration: in the Dalaran Visitor Center (52.2, 55.5), inspect the floor to the right of the entrance beside the small table/books.",
    "Illusion: near the Violet Hold entrance (64.5, 52.8), inspect the crate against the wall beside Archmage Timear. Do not enter the dungeon.",
    "Repeat only missing titles until all eight credit. Check your Toy Box for The Schools of Arcane Magic - Mastery: current comments report it can be learned directly rather than arriving by mail. Using that toy IN NORTHREND DALARAN and speaking to Vargoth gives the separate Familiar reward.",
},{pin(125,56.7,46.1,2,"Introduction - Violet Gate floor"),pin(125,30.9,46.3,3,"Conjuration - Citadel entrance floor"),pin(125,26.5,51.7,4,"Divination - Citadel UPSTAIRS"),pin(125,43.6,47.1,5,"Enchantment - Threads of Fate BALCONY"),pin(125,46.9,39.8,6,"Transmutation - Legerdemain DOWNSTAIRS"),pin(125,46.9,39.1,7,"Necromancy - Legerdemain UPSTAIRS bedroom"),pin(125,52.2,55.5,8,"Abjuration - Visitor Center floor"),pin(125,64.5,52.8,9,"Illusion - Violet Hold crate")},"Spawns can take hours and can produce decoys. A missing book today does not make the achievement retired; February 2026 replies confirm completion in 12.0.",{595175,1758359,1964160,6102467,6270986},"Exploration")
add(2557,"To All The Squirrels Who Shared My Life",{
    "Track the current checklist and use /love with each required animal targeted. These are emotes, not kill objectives. Summoned matching battle pets can satisfy several criteria; check those first, then visit the missing wild species below.",
    "Borean Tundra: /love a Borean Marmot near 51, 73 and a Tundra Penguin on the coast near 62, 68. Dragonblight: find an Arctic Hare around 28, 50; a plain Hare is a different name and is not a current criterion here.",
    "Sholazar Basin: /love a Sholazar Tickbird around Nesingwary Base Camp (27, 60). Icecrown: look for Glacier Penguins on the northern coast near 65, 22; current replies confirm they are present again after the old invasion phasing issue.",
    "Grizzly Hills: /love a Grizzly Squirrel around 43, 48 and a Mountain Skunk around 57, 35. Target the exact species rather than another nearby squirrel/skunk.",
    "Howling Fjord: /love a Fjord Penguin on the southwest coast (20, 60), a Scalawag Frog at Scalawag Point (35, 80), and a Fjord Turkey near Explorers' League Outpost (69.2, 64.6).",
    "For Huge Toad, use the Zul'Drak search area around 44, 61 (also found in the southern fields). Then travel to Searing Gorge and /love a tiny Lava Crab beside the lava at Pyrox Flats (42, 38). Check all twelve current species.",
},{pin(114,51,73,2,"Borean Marmot"),pin(114,62,68,2,"Tundra Penguin"),pin(115,28,50,2,"Arctic Hare"),pin(119,27,60,3,"Sholazar Tickbird"),pin(118,65,22,3,"Glacier Penguin - northern coast"),pin(116,43,48,4,"Grizzly Squirrel"),pin(116,57,35,4,"Mountain Skunk"),pin(117,20,60,5,"Fjord Penguin"),pin(117,35,80,5,"Scalawag Frog"),pin(117,69.2,64.6,5,"Fjord Turkey"),pin(121,44,61,6,"Huge Toad - search nearby"),pin(32,42,38,6,"Lava Crab - tiny critter beside lava")},"These are search areas, not guaranteed live spawns. The old temporary plain-Hare criterion and pre-Cataclysm Swamp of Sorrows coordinates are omitted.",{574766,1859107,3139945,3247577},"Exploration")
